WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.015 --> 00:00:01.860
(crowd noises)

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:04.333
- I had no idea what a bar mitzvah was.

00:00:05.290 --> 00:00:07.060
And then I saw it and I was like,

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:08.851
“Mama, why didn't you give me one?”

00:00:08.851 --> 00:00:11.100
(yelling, cheering)

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:13.360
And now I'm doing bar mitzvahs booked out

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:14.220
three years in advance.

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:15.430
You guys having a good time?

00:00:15.430 --> 00:00:17.750
My name is Kareem Wells,
and everybody call me

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:19.000
the King of the Mitzvahs.

00:00:23.126 --> 00:00:24.940
(quiet, intense music)

00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:27.480
I want to share a part of my heart,

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:28.750
and a part of my life.

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:32.160
When I was 16, I had my first kid.

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:33.810
I was kicked out of high school,

00:00:33.810 --> 00:00:36.690
so I did what most people my age did:

00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:38.003
I turned to the streets.

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:40.470
I started selling drugs.

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:43.630
I chose that because I felt
like I had no other option.

00:00:43.630 --> 00:00:45.340
I grew up on the west side of Chicago

00:00:45.340 --> 00:00:47.670
in a neighborhood where
there was a lot of violence,

00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:50.680
drug dealing, lot of illegal activity.

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:52.880
This is West Garfield Park,

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:54.520
and this is where my house used to be.

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:57.103
They tore it down, and it's just a lot.

00:00:58.150 --> 00:01:02.260
I had dreams, you know, of doing music,
and I loved performing.

00:01:02.260 --> 00:01:03.920
The OG's from the neighborhood,

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:06.110
they encouraged me to get out.

00:01:06.110 --> 00:01:07.870
They pushed me to follow my dream.

00:01:07.870 --> 00:01:10.020
- This guy, we knew he
was going to make it,

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:12.100
and he managed to pull that one off, man,

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:14.270
and I'm proud of the man.

00:01:14.270 --> 00:01:16.330
- The thing that the neighborhood gave me

00:01:16.330 --> 00:01:19.980
was toughness, and how
to hustle, never give up.

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:21.800
So when I'm out here
doing these bar mitzvahs,

00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:23.360
I'm gonna be strong with it.

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:24.480
You know, I’m going to give 200%.

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:25.880
I'm gonna be the best at it.

00:01:26.830 --> 00:01:27.930
Everybody here, right?

00:01:27.930 --> 00:01:29.160
Hey y'all, let's just meet real quick,

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:30.860
and just talk about what we goin' to do.

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:33.830
The way that I got involved
in the mitzvah business,

00:01:33.830 --> 00:01:38.020
I got a call one day from
a half-brother who told me

00:01:38.020 --> 00:01:39.940
that there was this party going on,

00:01:39.940 --> 00:01:42.000
and he said, "We need a dancer."

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:44.570
So I go over there, and
I see what's going on.

00:01:44.570 --> 00:01:47.000
I actually thought it was
a 50th birthday party.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:50.800
But it turns out that it was
a party for a 13-year-old boy.

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:52.410
Wassup, wassup?

00:01:52.410 --> 00:01:54.390
The people saw the way
we was doin' parties,

00:01:54.390 --> 00:01:56.200
the way we was bringing the energy,

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:58.569
the way we carried
ourselves with the kids,

00:01:58.569 --> 00:01:59.920
the way we carried
ourselves with the family.

00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:01.583
It was like, “We gotta get them.”

00:02:03.406 --> 00:02:05.903
One! Two!
Come on, clap your hands!

00:02:05.903 --> 00:02:06.881
Sing the words!

00:02:06.881 --> 00:02:07.990
Yo!
Hey!

00:02:07.990 --> 00:02:08.823
Let's go, right here!

00:02:08.823 --> 00:02:09.749
Are you ready?

00:02:09.749 --> 00:02:11.009
Jump to the beat!

00:02:11.009 --> 00:02:12.771
- [All] Everybody!

00:02:12.771 --> 00:02:15.973
(techno music)

00:02:15.973 --> 00:02:19.640
- Listen, when you walk
into a party that I'm MCing,

00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:22.940
you gonna feel the energy the
moment you walk in the room.

00:02:22.940 --> 00:02:26.620
And it's gonna be wild,
and crazy, and everybody's

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:28.050
going to be having the time of their life.

00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:29.300
We can celebrate.

00:02:29.300 --> 00:02:31.450
This about to be a crazy night.

00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:33.950
It'll be a memory that
that kid will never forget.

00:02:37.610 --> 00:02:40.670
You have some haters that
think it's kind of funny

00:02:40.670 --> 00:02:44.120
that a black kid from
the west side of Chicago

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:45.530
is doing bar mitzvahs.

00:02:45.530 --> 00:02:48.910
I say to them, “I’m the best in my shoes.”

00:02:48.910 --> 00:02:50.870
And I get to experience life at a level

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:53.050
that I never expected I would be.

00:02:53.050 --> 00:02:54.990
I never thought in a
million years that I would

00:02:54.990 --> 00:02:59.990
be the owner of a entertainment
company for bar mitzvahs.

00:03:00.210 --> 00:03:03.030
I am living proof that you
can come from absolutely

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:06.230
some very horrendous circumstances,

00:03:06.230 --> 00:03:07.800
and you can make something out of yourself

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:08.850
if you never give up.

00:03:11.210 --> 00:03:13.930
The success that this has brought me,

00:03:13.930 --> 00:03:17.150
it put me in a peaceful place.

00:03:17.150 --> 00:03:20.070
I'm getting paid to make people happy,

00:03:20.070 --> 00:03:22.473
to dance and sing, and I just feel great.

